                "text": "PA10-006u: In static initializers (module-level let bindings), & can only be applied directly to a symbol name, not to arbitrary expressions. For example, `let p: u64 = & target;` is valid, but `let p: u64 = & (expr);` is not. Address-of-expression patterns must be used in runtime contexts, not static initialization."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0230",
