              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 10 PA10-006y: The @align directive's value must be a positive integer that is a power of two, and must fit in the range [1, 2^30] (i.e., 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, ..., 1073741824). Common alignment values are 1, 4, 8, 16, 4096, 65536. Check that the value is a valid power of two and not too large."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0252",
              "id": "P0252",
              "name": "Invalid @align value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@align value must be a power of two in range [1, 2^30]"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 14 PA14-r14-008: The @ring directive is syntactically malformed. The correct syntax is '@ring(slots=N, slot_size=M)' where N and M are integer literals. N must be a power of two > 0, and M must be > 0. Either a required parameter is missing, the format is incorrect, or closing parentheses are missing. Example: `let mut ring_buf : [u64; 512] = uninit @ring(slots=256, slot_size=32)`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0253",
              "id": "P0253",
              "name": "Malformed @ring directive",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@ring(slots=N, slot_size=M) syntax error"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 14 PA14-r14-008: The @ring directive's slots parameter must be a positive integer that is a power of two. Valid slots values: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, etc. Check that the slots value is a power of two and not zero."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0260",
              "id": "P0260",
              "name": "Invalid @ring slots value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@ring slots must be a power of two and > 0"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 14 PA14-r14-008: The @ring directive's slot_size parameter must be a positive integer, and the total size (slots * slot_size) must not overflow a 64-bit integer. Check that slot_size is > 0 and not too large."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0261",
              "id": "P0261",
              "name": "Invalid @ring slot_size value or overflow",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@ring slot_size must be > 0 and not cause overflow"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression has an @ attribute that is not recognized. Valid attributes are @jump_table. Check the spelling of the attribute name."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0270",
              "id": "P0270",
              "name": "Unknown match attribute",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@<name> not recognized in match attributes"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression has a malformed @ attribute. The attribute name must be a valid identifier (e.g., @jump_table)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0271",
              "id": "P0271",
              "name": "Malformed match attribute",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match attribute syntax error"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression was marked with @jump_table but the coverage is too sparse (less than 50% density or range > 256). The elaborator will emit a cmp/je fallback chain instead of a dense jump table. To enable jump-table dispatch, ensure at least 50% coverage of the range and arm count <= 256."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0272",
              "id": "P0272",
              "name": "@jump_table density too sparse",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match is too sparse for jump-table codegen; reverting to cmp/je chain"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: This match has @jump_table set, but the full codegen (rodata synthesis + memory-indirect jmp) is deferred to issue pa-r15-009b. For now, the elaborator emits a cmp/je fallback chain. The jump-table dispatch will be implemented in a future release."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0273",
              "id": "P0273",
              "name": "@jump_table codegen deferred",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@jump_table codegen deferred to follow-up issue; using cmp/je fallback for now"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression marked with @jump_table lacks a default (_) arm. Jump-table dispatch requires an exhaustive default case for bounds-checking the dispatch index. Add a default arm with `_ => <expr>`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0274",
              "id": "P0274",
              "name": "@jump_table requires default arm",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match with @jump_table must have a default arm (_)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression marked with @jump_table has a non-integer-literal arm (e.g., a variable or string pattern). Jump-table dispatch requires all arms (except the default _) to be integer literals so the elaborator can compute density and generate the dispatch offset. Convert non-literal patterns to integer literals or remove @jump_table."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0275",
              "id": "P0275",
              "name": "@jump_table requires integer-literal arms",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match with @jump_table must have integer-literal patterns only"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1041: the current System-V x86-64 lowering passes lambda parameters in RDI, RSI, RDX, RCX, R8, R9. Stack-spill of the 7th+ parameter is not yet implemented. Reduce the parameter count to 6 or fewer, or split the function into curried groups (each group is a separate lambda)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0276",
              "id": "P0276",
              "name": "Lambda has more than 6 parameters",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "lambda arity exceeds System-V register-passed cap (6)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1071 (pa-r17-010b): A struct field declaration is syntactically incomplete. Ensure all fields follow the pattern `name: type`, separated by commas, with proper opening and closing braces. Trailing commas are allowed. Example: `struct S { x: u64, y: u32 }`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0277",
