            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010: The @link_section directive's name must be a valid identifier containing only letters, digits, dots, underscores, and hyphens. The name must be 1–32 characters long and non-empty. Example: `let payload : [u8; 8] = ... @link_section(\".uefi_hdr\")`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0282",
              "id": "P0282",
              "name": "Invalid @link_section name",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section name must match [A-Za-z0-9._-], length 1..32"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010: A let binding has multiple @link_section directives, which is not allowed. Remove all but one @link_section directive. Example: `let x = ... @link_section(\".foo\") @link_section(\".bar\")` is invalid."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0283",
              "id": "P0283",
              "name": "Duplicate @link_section directive",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section appears more than once on the same binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010 (MVP deferred to pa-r19-010b): The @link_section attribute is currently supported only on let bindings with data (literal, array) values. Lambda-shaped bindings (let x = fn(...)) are not yet supported. This is deferred to a future phase. Rewrite the binding without @link_section or defer the attribute."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0284",
              "id": "P0284",
              "name": "Lambda bindings cannot use @link_section",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section not yet supported on lambda-shaped let bindings"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-001: The @abi directive must specify a valid calling convention string. Valid options are \"ms\" (Microsoft x64 ABI for UEFI) and \"sysv\" (System V AMD64 ABI). The string must be lowercase, enclosed in double quotes, and passed as the sole argument to @abi. Examples: `@abi(\"ms\")` or `@abi(\"sysv\")`. Invalid strings, non-string arguments, missing parentheses, or empty strings all trigger this error."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0285",
              "id": "P0285",
              "name": "Invalid @abi(...) value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@abi requires \"ms\" or \"sysv\" (case-sensitive lowercase)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-001: The @abi calling-convention directive is intended for function-shaped bindings (lambdas). You have applied @abi to a let binding with a non-function value (literal, array, etc.). Remove the @abi directive or rewrite the binding as a lambda. Example: `let f = fn(...) -> ... @abi(\"ms\")` is valid, but `let x : u64 = 42 @abi(\"ms\")` is invalid."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0286",
              "id": "P0286",
              "name": "@abi directive only valid on function-shaped bindings",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@abi applied to non-lambda let binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010 (MVP deferred to pa-r19-010b): The @link_section attribute is currently supported only on let bindings with data (literal, array) values. Lambda-shaped bindings (let x = fn(...)) are not yet supported. This is deferred to a future phase. Rewrite the binding without @link_section or defer the attribute."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0287",
              "id": "P0287",
              "name": "Invalid @link_section for lambda binding",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section applied to lambda/function binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010: The @link_section attribute is not valid on mutable let bindings (let mut). Custom section placement is only supported for immutable data. If you need mutable data in a custom section, this is deferred to a future phase."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0288",
              "id": "P0288",
              "name": "@link_section requires immutable let binding",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section applied to mutable let binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-013 (pe-data-section-wiring): PE/COFF section names are limited to 8 bytes. The @link_section name you provided is longer than 8 bytes and cannot be emitted. Valid UEFI section names are `.text` (5 bytes), `.rdata` (6 bytes), `.data` (5 bytes), `.bss` (4 bytes), and custom names like `.uefi_hdr` (8 bytes), `.pdata` (6 bytes), `.xdata` (6 bytes), `.reloc` (6 bytes). Choose a shorter name or use a standard section."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0289",
