              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #980 (pa-r17-002): a let-binding annotated with a function-pointer type receives a value whose signature does not match. Signature matching requires: (1) equal arity, (2) invariant parameter types, (3) invariant return type, (4) source's effect row must be a subset of the target's (widening on assignment is safe; narrowing is not), (5) source's capability set must be a subset of the target's. The specific mismatch reason appears in the diagnostic's notes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/T0535",
              "id": "T0535",
              "name": "Function-pointer signature mismatch in assignment",
