            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1135 (pa-r17-016-followup): Pattern 5 module-level let-mut assignment via var_assign lowering accepts only Var-to-Var shapes where LHS is a module-level let-mut symbol (not shadowed by a local binding) and RHS is a function parameter (register) from local_bindings. Unsupported cases: (1) RHS is not a Var (e.g., literal, field access); (2) LHS is shadowed by a local binding; (3) LHS is not a module symbol; (4) structural invariants violated. For non-Var RHS patterns, use a separate let binding in the function body. For shadowed symbols, rename the local binding or restructure the scope."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/T0540",
