            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "visit_store requires each IrKind::Store node to carry exactly three children\n[addr, index_or_unused, value] with both addr and value materialized into\nIrKind::Var nodes by the ANF/let-hoisting pass. Any deviation — wrong child\ncount, non-Var addr, or non-Var value — indicates the parser/lowerer produced\na malformed Store: a post-elaboration invariant violation. Issue #1147 slice A2\nmigration from the legacy Vec<String> diagnostic channel to the typed pipe.\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1623",
              "id": "U1623",
              "name": "Malformed Store IR node: shape violates elaborator invariant",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Store node has wrong child count or non-Var addr/value after elaboration"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During IR traversal in emit_block_body / emit_block_body_arm, a RawInstruction\nchild node was encountered but the instruction payload was not found in the\nInstructionSideTable. Post-elaboration invariant violation: either the\ninstruction was not registered during elaboration or the side-table lookup\nfailed. Issue #1147 slice A3 migration from the legacy Vec<String> diagnostic\nchannel to the typed pipe (reclassified from T0526 to unsafe/invariant).\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1642",
              "id": "U1642",
              "name": "Instruction payload not found in side-table (invariant violation)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RawInstruction node lacks corresponding instruction payload"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During field-access elaboration, a Store, FieldAccess, or Deref node violated\na structural invariant. This can occur when:\n- A Store node has fewer than 3 children (expected: FieldAccess, index/unused, value)\n- A FieldAccess node has no child (expected: record value/Deref)\n- A Deref node has no child (expected: pointer)\n\nIssue #1147 slice A4 migration from the legacy Vec<String> diagnostic channel\nto the typed pipe. This diagnostic indicates a compiler-internal structural\ninvariant violation and should not occur in normal compilation.\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1643",
              "id": "U1643",
              "name": "Malformed field-shape IR node: shape violates elaborator invariant",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Store/FieldAccess/Deref node has wrong child count or missing required child"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During field-access lowering for a Store operation, a FieldAccess node was\nencountered but the corresponding FieldAccessInfo payload was not found in the\nside-table. This indicates an elaboration-phase invariant violation: either the\nFieldAccess node was not properly registered during elaboration, or the\nside-table lookup failed.\n\nIssue #1147 slice A4 migration from the legacy Vec<String> diagnostic channel\nto the typed pipe.\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1644",
              "id": "U1644",
              "name": "FieldAccessInfo side-table entry missing (invariant violation)",
