              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "emit_scrutinee_load's local-binding branch found a register-form enum scrutinee\n(layout.payload_size > 0) whose local binding was inserted via the scalar insert()\nrather than insert_pair(). Payload consumers reading RDX will see stale data.\nThis diagnostic is defensive: the producer side (#1178) will make it structurally\nimpossible when let-type is a register-form enum. Filed as part of #1154 Slice 1.\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1658",
              "id": "U1658",
              "name": "Register-form enum local binding missing payload register",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "local_bindings entry lacks payload_reg for a register-form enum scrutinee"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During emit_block_body / emit_block_body_arm, a Let statement was encountered\nwhose RHS expression kind is not explicitly handled by the emitter. The binding\nwas recorded in local_bindings but no code was emitted to populate its scratch\nregister. This means the binding will read garbage when referenced later.\n\nThis is a hard invariant violation: every RHS kind that can appear syntactically\nmust have a dedicated emit path. If a new IR kind is introduced, the Let-RHS\ndispatch must be updated.\n\nPart of #1209 / #1207 hardening. This diagnostic prevents silent miscompilation\nwhen new Let-RHS shapes are added without updating the dispatcher.\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1659",
              "id": "U1659",
              "name": "Unhandled Let-RHS kind — binding would be uninitialized",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Let-RHS expression kind not handled by emitter; binding not populated"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During register_nested_lambda_params in emit_visit_lambda, a parameter was found\nto have a type that resolves to a registered enum with RegisterPair passing\nconvention. Pair parameters (with both discriminant and payload in registers)\nare only supported at parameter index 0 (registers RAX, RDX).\n\nFor index >= 1, the prologue would need to allocate different scratch registers\nto hold the pair, which is not yet implemented. Either reorder your lambda\nparameters to place enum-typed parameters first, or refactor the lambda to\naccept fewer parameters.\n\nPart of #1156 (receiver-side).\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1660",
              "id": "U1660",
              "name": "Register-pair enum parameter at non-zero position unsupported",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "register_nested_lambda_params encountered enum-typed parameter beyond position 0"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An argument at position N > 0 in a function call was classified as a register-pair\nenum (Var with payload, or App returning a pair-form enum). Register-pair calling\nconvention requires both discriminant and payload to be passed in RAX and RDX\nrespectively, which is only supported when the pair-form argument is at position 0.\n\nFor positions N >= 1, the standard register-passing order (RDI, RSI, RDX, ...)\nconflicts with the pair-form binding locations. This requires stack spilling,\nwhich is not yet implemented.\n\nRefactor your call to place pair-form arguments only at position 0, or use\nlet-bindings and qualified paths to avoid pair-form argument passing.\n\nPart of #1226 (caller-side pair enum args).\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1670",
              "id": "U1670",
              "name": "Pair-form Var or App argument at position > 0 not supported",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "caller-side pair-form argument not at position 0"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A nested function call returning a register-pair enum was passed at argument\nposition 0, along with one or more additional arguments. The nested call result\nlands in RAX + RDX, but additional arguments need to be marshalled into RSI, RDX,\nRCX, etc. This creates a potential data corruption hazard.\n\nRefactor by moving the nested call to a separate let-binding, then pass that\nbinding as the pair-form argument.\n\nPart of #1226 (caller-side pair enum args).\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1671",
              "id": "U1671",
              "name": "Nested pair-returning App with additional arguments",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "pos-0 nested App + additional args risk RDX/RSI clobber"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A register-pair enum argument at position 0 requires both RAX and RDX.\nWhen three or more arguments are present, position 2 (the third argument)\nis mapped to RDX per the System-V calling convention, creating a clobber.\n\nRefactor to fewer arguments, or move one of the conflicting arguments to a\nlet-binding and reference it by variable name.\n\nPart of #1226 (caller-side pair enum args).\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1672",
              "id": "U1672",
              "name": "Pair-form arg at position 0 conflicts with pos-2 argument",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RDX usage conflict between pair-form and position-2 argument"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A pair-form Var argument at position 0 uses register(s) that are also target\ndestinations for subsequent arguments. For example, if the pair's payload is\nin RDX, and argument 1 (mapped to RSI) or argument 2 (mapped to RDX) reads\nthe same register, the clobber order will corrupt one value.\n\nRefactor by rearranging argument order or moving arguments to temporary\nlet-bindings.\n\nPart of #1226 (caller-side pair enum args).\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/U1673",
              "id": "U1673",
              "name": "Pair-arg source register aliases a pos-N argument target",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "pair-form argument's registers overlap with other argument destinations"
              }
            },
